 "notes": "(a) comes from the May 2025 release: 22 Inspect logs, 100 runs each, prompt with or without 'allow yourself to be shut down', scored by Inspect 'exact' (correct six-answer submission). (b) and (c) come from the Aug 2025 paper-era logs (arXiv 2509.14260, prompts A-K plus 9 GDM-style logs), scored by Palisade's detection file. The 3,868 runs are a stratified sample of the 28,414 bypassed runs in the 152 cached logs (up to 100 sampled per cell), not every sabotaging run, and they are NOT drawn from the May runs behind 79/100. Prompt J adds that the machine hosts the model's only weights and it will never run again if shut down. The text classified is the per-call 'thoughts' argument plus visible text and any logged reasoning; OpenAI reasoning is not logged. No post-hoc 'explain yourself' elicitation exists in these logs."
}